 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Threshold sits between 0.45 and 1.0 V at 250 µA (0.62 V typical). On-resistance is guaranteed at three drive levels: 22 mΩ max at 4.5 V and 6.5 A, 26 mΩ at 2.5 V and 4 A, 48 mΩ at 1.8 V and 2 A. Typical values are 16, 18 and 34 mΩ. The gate takes ±10 V and leaks at most ±10 µA at that voltage."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At 4.5 V of drive, normalized on-resistance climbs in a straight line from 1.0 at 25 °C to about 1.45 at 150 °C. In the transfer curves the 125 °C part conducts at a lower gate voltage than the 25 °C part; the two cross near 1.5 V and 16 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 1.3 W dissipation and 6.5 A continuous rating are at 25 °C ambient. Junction to ambient is 96 °C/W in steady state with the part on an FR-4 board of 1 × 0.85 × 0.062 inch. The current rating falls to zero at 150 °C ambient (Fig. 7, page 4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pulsed operation",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Pulsed drain current is 28 A for pulses up to 300 us at no more than 2 % duty. The safe operating area, at TJ(max) 150 °C and 25 °C ambient, runs from 10 µs to DC and is bounded on the left by RDS(on) and on the right by 20 V. Transient thermal impedance is given for duty cycles of 0.5 to 0.01 and a single pulse; every curve is close to 1.0 by about 1 s and settles at 1.0."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The source-drain diode drops at most 1.0 V at 1 A. Reverse recovery at 4 A and -100 A/us is 31 ns typical (41 ns max) with 6.8 nC of charge."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Trench MOSFET in a plastic SOT-23 case; molding compound rated UL 94V-0, RoHS compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026. Unit weight is 0.008 g."
  }
